From: Michael Stufflebeam <cpuchip@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:49:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 065: MINES revision 2, the settings: listed at stu32-arcade
 7344045, its board script

Three boards (easy 9x9/10, medium 16x16/40, hard 30x16/99), classic rules and the
game's sound on a settings page (Michael's decisions 76 and 77); the first open's
deal runs across ticks, 4 attempts a tick with the cap at 400, so the hard board's
slowest deal (1.77 s on the S3) never blocks a key. +1,792 B flash on the stand-in,
+1,808 on Rev A, +0 internal RAM; S3 DEVICE PASS (eight scripts' frames = host, the
control red); work/065-mines-rev2.md has the checks and the numbers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
